LeetCode 48 – Rotate Image
Problem Description

Given an n × n 2D matrix representing an image, rotate the image 90 degrees clockwise.

The rotation must be done in-place, meaning you must modify the input matrix directly without creating another matrix.

Approach: Transpose + Reverse

This solution uses two operations to rotate the matrix 90 degrees clockwise:

Transpose the Matrix: Swap elements across the main diagonal.
Reverse Each Row: Reverse every row of the transposed matrix.

Combining these two operations produces a 90-degree clockwise rotation without using extra matrix space.

Example

Input:

python
matrix = [
    [1, 2, 3],
    [4, 5, 6],
    [7, 8, 9]
]


Output:

python
[
    [7, 4, 1],
    [8, 5, 2],
    [9, 6, 3]
]

Step-by-Step Explanation

Step 1: Original Matrix

text
1 2 3
4 5 6
7 8 9


Step 2: Transpose the Matrix

Swap elements across the main diagonal.

text
1 4 7
2 5 8
3 6 9


Step 3: Reverse Each Row

text
7 4 1
8 5 2
9 6 3


The matrix is now rotated 90 degrees clockwise.

Complexity Analysis

Let n be the number of rows (and columns) in the square matrix.

Time Complexity: O(n²) – Transposing visits the upper triangular portion of the matrix, and reversing each row takes O(n²) overall.
Space Complexity: O(1) – The rotation is performed in-place without using any additional matrix.
Key Takeaway

A 90-degree clockwise matrix rotation can be achieved efficiently using two simple operations:

Transpose the matrix.
Reverse each row.

This is an optimal in-place solution with O(n²) time complexity and O(1) auxiliary space.
